Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, python3 (>= 3.12), python3-psycopg, python3-yaml, python3-cryptography, maluos-firstboot (>= 0.1.12), maluos-vault (>= 0.4.2), maluos-estate (>= 0.5.0)
Recommends: maluos-agent (>= 0.6.0)
Description: MaluOS memory face: scoped memory for local principals and the estate
 Every MaluOS host is a memory host (its MaluDB tenant, the principals and
 scopes of its agents). The face is the one service that opens principal-
 bound sessions on it (Phase 13 slice 4, docs/phase13-slice4-memory.md):
 over /run/maluos/memory.sock it answers local principals, identified by
 their uid (recall, remember, forget, usage); over the overlay (port 11437,
 `maluctl memory expose`) it answers the estate: a query carries a slice 2
 envelope, the face verifies it against the peers the office publishes,
 intersects the delegated scopes with what this host shares (`maluctl
 memory share`, the guest principal's grants and ceiling), and answers
 claims: the memory's text with its scope, sensitivity, confidence, time,
 source and holder, never the record behind it. `maluctl memory recall
 --estate` asks every holder the office publishes for the scopes asked;
 `maluctl memory sync` copies the summaries a rule lets this host replicate,
 provenance kept. Every query answered or asked is one ledger row with the
 scopes and the counts, never the text.
